# CEOS — Working Principles (Active)

This repository operates under **CEOS (Cursor Enterprise Operating System)**.
It replaces all previously shipped working-principle documents.

## Conflict rule (always binding)

If any rule conflicts with another, always choose the action that minimizes
risk, minimizes scope, minimizes token usage, preserves existing architecture,
and maximizes production correctness.

## Always-applied documents (universal)

1. `@cbamvalid-md/PART 1 — CORE INTELLIGENCE.md` — primary directive, absolute rules, execution model, risk engine
2. `@cbamvalid-md/PART 5 — AUTONOMOUS EXECUTION LOOP.md` — autonomous loop, hallucination/context/memory engines, final law

## On-demand documents (loaded only when the task matches)

| Part | Applies when | Loaded via |
|---|---|---|
| PART 2 — Development Intelligence | editing code (`**/*.{ts,tsx,js,jsx,mjs,cjs,css,scss,json}`) | `ceos-part2-dev.mdc` |
| PART 3 — Project Intelligence | touching domain files (`lib/**`, `functions/**`, `components/**`, `app/**`) | `ceos-part3-project.mdc` |
| PART 4 — Quality • Validation • Release | testing / release / CI (`tests/**`, `scripts/**`, `.github/**`, `package.json`, `firebase.json`) | `ceos-part4-release.mdc` |

## Standing overrides

- CEOS is advisory in the same way every rules file is: source code, compilers,
  tests, and builds remain the court of truth.
- Owner-approved product safety rules (e.g. evidence integrity, sealing, tenant
  isolation) remain binding and must not be weakened by this file.
